---
title: Transfer Funds - how ACID is achieved (ledger_transfer)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer (bank_client)
    participant S as Server child process
    participant G as Gate (.gate)
    participant F as customers.dat
    participant T as transactions.dat
    participant J as journal/jnl_pid.dat

    C->>S: Request{OP_TRANSFER, to=1002, amount}
    Note over S: role checked from SESSION,<br/>not from the request
    S->>G: fcntl F_RDLCK (shared)
    S->>F: fcntl F_WRLCK record 1001 (lower id first)
    S->>F: fcntl F_WRLCK record 1002
    Note over S,F: ISOLATION - other processes touching<br/>1001/1002 now wait (F_SETLKW)
    S->>J: any orphan journal of a dead process?
    S->>F: lseek + read both records
    Note over S: CONSISTENCY checks:<br/>both ACTIVE, balance >= amount,<br/>target exists, not self
    S->>T: append 2 records as PENDING (append lock)
    S->>J: write before + after images
    S->>J: fsync()  (write-ahead)
    S->>F: write debit 1001, write credit 1002
    S->>T: flip both records to COMMITTED
    S->>F: fsync()
    S->>T: fsync()
    S->>J: unlink()  = COMMIT point
    Note over S,J: ATOMICITY - a crash before this point<br/>leaves the journal, recovery restores<br/>the before images (all or nothing)
    S->>F: unlock 1002, 1001
    S->>G: unlock
    S-->>C: Response{OK, new balance}
    Note over C,S: DURABILITY - "OK" is sent only<br/>after fsync() of every file
